===Verb===
{{en-verb}}

# {{lb|en|transitive}} To [[throw]] (something) at a [[high speed]].
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2004|author=Richard Marinick|chapter=25|title=Boyos: A Novel|location=Boston, Mass.|publisher=Kate’s Mystery Books|page=112|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/boyosnovel00mari/page/112/mode/1up|isbn=1-932112-32-4|passage=Kevin pushed away from the desk and '''fastballed''' it into the other man’s chest.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|date=6 December 2007|author=w:Jennifer Rardin|chapter=5|title=Another One Bites the Dust|series=[[w:Jaz Parks series|Jaz Parks]]|seriesvolume=2|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Orbit Books|Orbit]]|page=44|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/anotheronebitesd00rard/page/44/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-316-02057-2|passage=Wyatt spurred his horse to the middle of the stones, reached into the corpse’s chest, yanked out the heart, and '''fastballed''' it at a vine-covered tree stump.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=2014|author=Kenneth Calhoun|chapter=15|title=Black Moon: A Novel|location=New York, N.Y.|publisher=[[w:Hogarth Press|Hogarth]]|page=240|pageurl=https://archive.org/details/blackmoonnovel0000calh/page/240/mode/1up|isbn=978-0-8041-3714-0|passage=He targeted a man standing a bit taller than the others and '''fastballed''' the lock in his direction. The lock somehow managed to miss everyone below and clattered against the pavement.}}

